troparia.text:
Once Saul crouched like a lion, wrathfully destroyed the Church of Christ;
but he was seized by the divine voice of the Lamb of God, Whom he had persecuted,
and Who entrusted His flock to him as a shepherd.

As is meet, Damascus is given drink by Paul;
for from him, as from the garden of paradise,
a great well-spring of divine waters once issued forth
and irrigated the whole earth abundantly with divine knowledge.

ode6.irmos2:
I will pour out my prayer unto the Lord,
and to Him will I proclaim my grief;
for my soul is filled with evils,
and my life unto Hades hath drawn nigh,
and like Jonah I pray unto Thee:
Raise me up from corruption, O God.

troparia.text:
Thou didst forsake things which were not essential, O Peter,
and attain unto those things which are essential;
and like a merchant thou didst manifestly search for Christ: the Pearl beyond price.

As an excellent emulator of the Master, clothed in Him, O Paul,
thou wast truly all things to all men, that thou mightest acquire and save all the people;
and pursuing the ends of the world for Christ, thou didst truly save them.

As is meet Christ hath given thee life in the heavens, O Apostle Paul;
for thou didst not desire a city which abideth here, O blessed one,
but wast a faithful minister and celebrant of His mysteries.

Theotokion: The Lord looked down upon thee, restoring my nature, in that He is mighty;
and doing mighty works, O all-immaculate Birthgiver of God,
through thee my God hath saved me from corruption, in that He is full of loving-kindness.

Working wonders, by the word of grace thou didst heal Eneus who was grievously paralyzed,
and didst raise up Tabitha from the dead;
wherefore they cried: Bless the Lord, all ye works of the Lord!

Paul was bound to thee by Thy love and underwent a goodly change;
for the glorious one lived not for himself, O Compassionate One,
but had Thee living within him throughout all ages.

Thou didst betroth the Church unto Christ, presenting it to Him as a bride;
for thou wast shown to be its wedding-escort, O God-bearing Paul.
Wherefore, it glorifieth thee throughout all ages.

Thine excellent grace is rightly glorified,
for thy very shadow dispelleth the sufferings of the sick, O Peter;
wherefore, we magnify thee.

Theotokion: O most holy Mother of God,
thou wast the boast of the apostles of Christ, the glory of the martyrs and the foundation of the prophets;
wherefore, we all magnify thee as is meet.
